  <item>
    <title><![CDATA[Light Dark Toggle]]></title>
    <dc:creator><![CDATA[admin]]></dc:creator>
    <content:encoded><![CDATA[<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Use the switch in the header to change between light and dark mode. Your choice is saved in this browser, so it stays when you reload the page.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The block only adds or removes the <code>wpcomsp-light-dark-active</code> class on the <code>&lt;html></code> element. This demo pairs it with a few lines of Additional CSS (Site Editor → Styles → Additional CSS) that swap the theme’s base and contrast colours while the class is present.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:group {"style":{"spacing":{"padding":{"top":"var:preset|spacing|40","bottom":"var:preset|spacing|40","left":"var:preset|spacing|40","right":"var:preset|spacing|40"}}},"backgroundColor":"accent-5","layout":{"type":"constrained"}} -->
<div class="wp-block-group has-accent-5-background-color has-background" style="padding-top:var(--wp--preset--spacing--40);padding-right:var(--wp--preset--spacing--40);padding-bottom:var(--wp--preset--spacing--40);padding-left:var(--wp--preset--spacing--40)"><!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">A sample section</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Text, backgrounds and buttons all follow the theme colour palette, so they change together when you toggle the mode.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:buttons -->
<div class="wp-block-buttons"><!-- wp:button -->
<div class="wp-block-button"><a class="wp-block-button__link wp-element-button">Primary button</a></div>
<!-- /wp:button -->

<!-- wp:button {"className":"is-style-outline"} -->
<div class="wp-block-button is-style-outline"><a class="wp-block-button__link wp-element-button">Outline button</a></div>
<!-- /wp:button --></div>
<!-- /wp:buttons --></div>
<!-- /wp:group -->

<!-- wp:quote -->
<blockquote class="wp-block-quote"><!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Dark mode is easier on the eyes at night; light mode is easier to read in daylight.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></blockquote>
<!-- /wp:quote -->]]></content:encoded>
